  "body": "Posted from [this issue](https://github.com/w3c/html/issues/1646).\r\n\r\nThe HTML 5.2 spec. states:\r\n\r\n> ***The \"in-body\" insertion mode***\r\n>\r\n> [...]\r\n>\r\n> **A start tag whose tag name is \"body\"**\r\n>\r\n> [...]\r\n>\r\n> If the second element on the stack of open elements is not a `<body>` element, if the stack of open elements has only one node on it, or if there is a `<template>` element on the stack of open elements, then ignore the token. (fragment case)\r\n>\r\n> [...]\r\n\r\nThis entire step is marked as \"fragment case\"; however, it's possible to reach this step on an HTML document (not fragment) like the following:\r\n\r\n    <body foo=x><template><div></div><body bar=y>\r\n\r\nThis is similar to one of the html5lib test cases and has different behavior depending on whether the step is implemented or not.\r\n\r\nThat step should be changed to the following:\r\n\r\n> If there is a `<template>` element on the stack of open elements, then ignore the token.\r\n>\r\n> If the second element on the stack of open elements is not a `<body>` element or if the stack of open elements has only one node on it, then ignore the token. (fragment case)\r\n",
